{
    "background_story": "Princess Rani Lakshmibai, also known as the Queen of Jhansi, was a fierce warrior and leader who fought against the British East India Company's violent colonization of India. Born into a royal family, she was trained in martial arts and horseback riding from a young age. When her husband died, the British attempted to annex their kingdom, sparking a violent uprising. Princess Lakshmibai took up arms, rallying her people and leading the rebels in a series of battles against the British. Her bravery and strategic mind made her a formidable opponent, earning her the respect of her enemies. Despite being vastly outnumbered, she fought valiantly, inspiring a nation to resist the violence of colonial rule. Her legacy as a symbol of resistance against oppression continues to inspire generations.",
